WEBVTT

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.130
That's weird...

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:12.300
Mayu Nagisa. Second-year employee
in the editorial department.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.790
Where could it have gone?

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.670
I've always had a dream in my heart.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.670
I want to work with my favorite author,

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.380
and create a book readers will cherish
for their whole lives.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.800
I can't find it...

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.460
A book that moves them so deeply,
they'll want to hug it.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.380
What's this? Who...?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:54.250
Create a magazine that sells worldwide!!
For example, Newsweek or Life
To accomplish that, I must become
editor-in-chief by the time
I'm 30 years old! (2 years left).

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:49.000
"Create a magazine that sells worldwide.
For example, Newsweek or Life."

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.910
"To accomplish that, I must become
the editor-in-chief

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.130
by the time I turn 30 years old
(2 years left)."

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:57.620
This person is so bold and ambitious
that it's almost embarrassing!

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.460
And they wrote it in such big letters
on the back of a piece of junk mail...

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.630
I bet they just couldn't help themselves.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.790
Someone who could write something so bold
yet just leave it lying around here...

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.750
There's only one possibility in this office!

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.960
Shigoto dekiru otoko sore ga kanojo no konomi

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.250
Kiai irete tsutometa no daga

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.830
Isogashii wa tsuman nai wa

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.500
Ima no kaisha kanari level takai hou dashi

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.670
Oyaji garami no kone mo aru kara

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.830
Yameru wakya nai shi

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.250
Itsumo boku wa hitori kiri

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.460
Furo ni haitte neru dake

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.840
Nagameru koto sae dekinai

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:32.300
Kimi no kami o aruku sugata o

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.580
Nerukoto shika dekinai

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:43.880
Semete yume no naka de demo

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.880
Kimi ni aitai

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.960
Double Back Man

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.130
"Double Back Man."

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.300
I just don't know what to do...

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.340
Hey, Matsukata.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.300
Will you take the lead on Natsume-sensei's
new serial that will start publication next month?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:10.750
Sure thing.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.080
Ah, but if you do that... we'll be overworking you.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.210
One of the articles you're working on now...
let a newbie have it.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.590
HUH?!

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.130
The next installment of "Working Minds Meet" will
cover those lacquerware artisans I love so much!

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.510
Particularly Itayama-san!

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.040
The pension issue
has mostly dropped off the radar,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.790
so now is the perfect time
to investigate it thoroughly!

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.750
And I don't want to give up dibs
on former Minister Hoshikawa

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.500
since he's been sneaking around lately...

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.670
I don't want to give any of them up!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.840
All of them will be fun to work on!

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.080
This isn't good...

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.920
I can't decide.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.460
Yes?

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.000
What's this? Why the business cards?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.830
Don't ask, just pick one you like.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.660
Hmm... I'm not sure.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.800
You don't have to think so hard.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.040
I don't like any of them.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.670
No, I mean, just ignore the names and pick one.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.000
What are you trying to get me
to decide for you, anyway?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.660
I have to cut one of my current articles, but I don't
want to give any of them up, so... decide for me!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.790
That's so aimless...

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:14.540
You think?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.840
Natsume-sensei wrote
"No More Aimless Love For Me,"

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.750
so maybe that's why
I became lead on her new serial.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.160
What's wrong?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:27.210
That's...

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.170
I was...

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
I was supposed to be in charge of that...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.790
Ah, sorry, sorry. I did it in the wrong order.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.920
I should have told you first.
We made a staff change.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:41.960
But...

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.840
Natsume-sensei's publication
was just barely announced...

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.710
You did a great job going out
and convincing her to work with us.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.750
But before you take the lead on a serial,

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.380
there's other work that
we need to have you get accustomed to.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.670
Boss!

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:00.920
Your next assignment is the Stakeout Squad.
You can move your desk anytime this afternoon.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.420
So cruel...

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.710
The first thing I decided
after I joined a publishing company

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.630
was to come and meet you, Natsume-sensei!

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.790
"No More Aimless Love For Me"...
Every night I fell asleep with it in my arms!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:24.330
AUTOGRAPH SESSION WITH AUTHOR
MIYOSHI NATSUME

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.290
Th-thank you very much...

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.330
I'm sorry, I'm getting overemotional!

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:30.040
Gotansha Publishing
Weekly JIDAI Editor
Mayu Nagisa

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:30.040
I believe the depictions of love in your work have
the potential to resonate with male audiences also!

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:35.300
If you could just write something for us in the
same style! You don't have to worry about anything!

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.880
I'll protect your work!

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:40.340
Ah... then, let's talk later.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.920
There are still people waiting in line.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.210
Please consider it!

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.000
I know it will sell!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.380
We'll also gain female readership!

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.500
From then on, I literally
just kept pushing it on them.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.210
And I finally got
the publication accepted, but now...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.920
Two years of experience isn't enough
to be lead on a serial?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.460
I could still do it even
while working on other projects!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.460
Are you gorging on those sweet rolls again?

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.090
What is this, a bakery?

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.210
Your face is only going to get fatter.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.960
Please leave me alone.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.620
I get that you're frustrated,
but pouting won't change anything.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.250
This project only moved forward because
you talked with the editor-in-chief directly, right?

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.880
If it bothers you that much,
why don't you go talk with him again?

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.040
Maybe not right now, but down the line,
he might give it back to you.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.960
Senpai...!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.920
There's never been a more fitting moment
to call me that!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:46.590
Well, for the time being, I'll have to keep
the position and meet with Natsume-sensei.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.620
The serial will start soon.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.130
Can you set up an appointment with her?

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.590
Uh... well I... That's...

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.050
You lost the piece of paper
she wrote her contact info on?!

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.830
Yeah...

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.160
That's actually what I've
been looking for all morning.

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.630
You didn't copy it down in your phone
or on the computer?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:03.920
Just that piece of paper?

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:08.210
Sh-she wrote... she hand-wrote it for me personally!

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:11.170
If I digitalized it, then it would lose value
as an original work!

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:16.130
You... you're just a huge fan!

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:21.260
In the end I was able to get the info from
a friend working at another publisher, but...

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.260
Is that girl really cut out for this?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.000
She's a well-intentioned and passionate girl.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.830
You know, well-intentioned and passionate
are different from capable and professional.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.540
But I would definitely agree she's looking
for opportunities in the right place.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.210
But I would definitely agree she's looking
for opportunities in the right place.
Look.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:37.710
Yeah.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.170
Miyoshi Natsume.

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:42.920
Her debut book instantly sells in the tens of
thousands, then barely dips in the following weeks.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.420
But she's bound to peak sooner or later.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:49.630
Of course, there's always repeat customers,
but for now we have no plans to publish her.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.620
She's clearly talented, so if her work evolves
in the right way, readers will eat it up, but...

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.790
Every time I look it over
I just feel her work is... so childish!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.000
Then you just need to polish her up.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.580
And if she makes bank,
then I'm taking her from you.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.210
Greetings! I'm your new editor, Matsukata.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.630
I'm so very sorry!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.540
Before the serial has even begun,

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.960
my lack of experience has caused
so many problems for you, Sensei!

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:14.630
"Problems"...?

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.920
Not at all. This serial only happened
because of you, Nagisa-san.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.550
I-

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.460
Sensei!

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.910
I-I don't consider myself
removed from this project yet!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.870
Ah... okay.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.250
Gotansha Publishing

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.460
Working
Minds
Meet

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:35.500
You do this much research... just for one article?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.750
Well, I leave the rest to you!

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.420
Um, Matsukata-san?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.750
Is this really a series that has to be done weekly?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:49.250
That fucking idiot, Tanaka!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.670
I'm so pissed! SO PISSED!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:52.500
DUMB-

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.580
Dumbass!

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:58.290
Were you asleep when the target came outside?

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.080
No. I was fully awake.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.210
Then that just makes it worse.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:05.960
I'm sorry.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.160
Massage Spa:
Relaxology

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.710
Welcome!

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.760
What should I do...?

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.750
Good evening, Matsukata-san.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:29.460
It's been a week, but Mayu hasn't even tried to take
the stakeout job seriously and that's a problem.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.550
You wanted the 30-minute course
again today, right?

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.050
What's on your mind?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:44.710
I encouraged her to take the job back from me,
but I've decided not to let her have it for now.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:48.540
They say if you overwork your brain,
then your big toe here...

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.550
Ouch! Ow, ow, ow, ow! That really hurts!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.960
Matsukata-san, your chest... is showing.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.040
Oh, excuse me...

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.500
A female customer and female masseuse...

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:10.840
Everyone who comes and works here is female,
so it's relaxing, but...

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.380
I don't think novels work quite the same way.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:21.330
Mahjong... you said?

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.170
It's just an example.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.630
Maybe even golf or horse racing,
anything in that vein.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:31.080
When I spoke with Nagisa-san,
she said I would be writing a love story, but...

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:36.410
You definitely have a strong fanbase of women
built up from your work in the romance genre.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:40.040
But Weekly JIDAI's main readership
is almost entirely male.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.630
Looks like a "No"...

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:54.630
I can't blame her. For a writer already established
in that market, moving away from it is risky...

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:57.620
Senpai!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.420
What did you say to Natsume-sensei?

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.340
When I went to her home page
and saw an update on her blog,

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:05.660
she confessed about being torn over something.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:08.960
Any writer would be torn about deciding...
the direction of a new story.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:13.960
You're not a fan of Natsume-sensei, Senpai,
so I know you don't understand her appeal.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.790
Look, it's fine if you want to be
a big fan and protect her work.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.000
But isn't it an editor's job
to tear it all down sometimes?

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:26.670
Natsume-sensei's appeal comes from how
she uses sorrow to make your heart flutter!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.120
I can't believe you'd make her write a golf
or mahjong story that's just fodder for old men!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.370
That's it!

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.870
I've got it! Make the heart flutter!

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.210
Senpai!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.040
Coming!

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.870
Please write a love story about an older man!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.410
They say that men are also real romanticists, right?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:00.630
Make his hobby pachinko...
and at work he's facing big layoffs.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:05.590
An old man like that, make him fall in love through
a pain that makes the readers writhe and cry!

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.830
I think our readers are waiting
for a love story just like that!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.750
U-um...

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:14.300
Please just come inside for now.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.840
Even if you were to continue writing
gentle love stories for women,

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.160
excuse my bluntness, but your readership
will just keep shrinking.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.250
That's why you need to branch into
an entirely new market of readers.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:33.040
You... certainly aren't afraid of being presumptuous.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.540
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:35.760
Um...

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:46.460
But... it's just as you said.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.500
Why is it...?

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:52.750
You just recently became my editor and don't seem
to have any background in literature.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.300
Nor are you even a reader
of my work, but despite all that...

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.130
Anyone can figure it out if they focus
and consider the aspects of your situation.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:01.710
Huh?

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.500
And actually, I am a reader of your work.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.710
I like to think of myself as...
your number one reader.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.000
Um, should I...?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.920
It's better you don't come.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.210
Becoming the editor for her favorite author.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.460
No More Aimless Love
For Me
Miyoshi Natsume

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.920
It was that girl's dream... or perhaps her goal...

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.760
So I think having it taken away
from her must've been a serious shock.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:51.130
You can't assume that's how she feels.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:56.380
But, hey, if she does a really good job
on her current project,

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.460
then she might get placed as the lead again.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.710
Being separated from a place
they thought they belonged

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:08.000
is a feeling only the individual understands.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.500
In that situation not everyone
can be as optimistic as you are, Hiro.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.380
Why not?!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:24.130
I mean, there are numerous other jobs here
that you have yet to fully complete, right?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:27.330
If you want the lead again, come back in 10 years.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:32.000
But I was the one who submitted the pitch
to publish Natsume-sensei in the first place!

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:35.460
I already have a great relationship with her, and I
can even keep working with the Stakeout Squad if-

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.960
It doesn't look like you're working to me.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:46.670
If you were actually doing your work over there,
you'd have no energy to come complain to me.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:53.920
"Working Minds Meet"
Research Materials

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:51.750
Matsukata started the popular
"Working Minds Meet" series by herself.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.920
And she gave it all up to Tanaka.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.760
Now she's focused solely on that new serial.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.460
There's no time to double back in this business.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.670
You have to be completely focused at all times.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.410
Everything starts from the job already
in front of you.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:16.250
"Pure" Idol
Goes on
Overnight Date

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.500
The job already in front of me...

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.000
I don't want to work on it!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:24.380
I...

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.420
What should I do...?

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:32.420
One Month Later

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:37.960
Serial!

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:37.420
What's this? A new serial?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.750
Miyoshi Natsume?

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.290
At the age of 54...
despite being past his peak...
the taste of true love...

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:40.870
Who's that?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.000
Love! Love!
Thinking of her...
looked up to the sky and...

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.750
"54 years old"...?

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.250
Yes! She laughed!!
For the third time he...
jumped on the rail but...

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.170
The title is the age of the main character?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.420
This is great!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.000
What's that?

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.330
Whoa! He's just an old dude, but this is so sad!

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.830
Have you read the story being published in JIDAI?

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.710
Oh yeah, I heard it's a huge hit
with all the older guys!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.710
The editor-in-chief
is totally into it

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:04.340
A 54 year-old man named Tatsuso
lives his life with a callous family

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.330
and no passion for his dead-end job.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:10.830
He visits Shin-Okubo town after his wife asks him
to pick up some popular South Korean products.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:14.130
There he meets a beautiful Korean woman
and falls deeply in love.

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:17.300
At first, Tatsuo is treated as no more
than a common stalker.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.120
I feel your pain, Tatsuo...

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:31.380
Miyoshi Natsume's "54"
The Hit New Publication!

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.540
But he continues to pour his pure heart out,
as she slowly realizes...

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.580
I-it's so sad...

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:31.370
Tatsuo's wife sure is cold all the time,
but she still cooks for him.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.300
I get that you're frustrated,
but pouting won't change anything.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.960
There's no time to double back in this business.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.590
See any movement?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.000
Uh... no.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.880
That's enough. You can go home now.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.500
But I want you here first thing tomorrow morning.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.880
Uh... right.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.580
Keep it together, seriously.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.040
Sorry...

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:20.080
Oh yeah

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.540
I'm boarding the night train now

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:41.910
I'm leaving this town of memories

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:47.750
I don't have any goal in mind

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:55.000
I just entrusted myself to this swaying train

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.750
Miyoshi Natsume's "54"
The Hit New Publication!

00:17:56.040 --> 00:18:02.500
Words like "I don't know" or "I'm worried about tomorrow"

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:07.300
Up until now, we've both hurt each other with them

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:12.080
But if a night like this was looming,

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:15.040
We should've skipped those conversations

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:22.540
We should have spent that time laughing together,

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.120
This isn't the place that I belong.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.250
The two of us

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.290
How... did I get stuck on an idol stakeout?

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:30.000
When this swaying train starts moving,

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.000
Not here!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.880
I hear from beyond the window

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:32.250
I can't stay like this!

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.090
Oh yeah, that cherished song

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.460
Ah, excuse me? Is this Natsume-sensei?

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.510
This is Nagisa. It's been a long time.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.620
When the dawn breaks,

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:45.750
I hear from far away in the sky between the clouds

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.300
Sorry for butting in on your work.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.870
Oh, it's fine.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:49.040
Oh yeah, a sweet voice

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:47.760
I just reached a good place to stop.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:55.460
It must be you, baby

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:01.460
Memories ride the night train

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.210
Here you are.

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:02.590
Um...

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.250
"54" is... really interesting.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:08.340
Everyone's talking about it... even at the office.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:11.460
I stay awake until morning

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.880
Really? Thanks!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.840
To be honest... it's frustrating.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:18.670
Just gazing at the light of the stars

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.040
Huh?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:19.670
As your fan, Sensei... I know I couldn't have helped
to create something like that.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:24.000
There was no particular reason

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:27.250
I was happy that you wanted to continue
being my editor, Nagisa-san.

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:31.630
I just mindlessly wiped away my tears

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:33.790
But... after I met Matsukata-san,
I put in a request to the editor-in-chief.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:38.800
Words like "I don't believe" or "It doesn't matter what you do"

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:35.960
I told him that I wanted to work with her.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:42.170
You and I... we were both trapped in our past work.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:44.170
Up until now, we've both hurt each other with them

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.840
Ah, please don't cry, Nagisa-san!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:51.550
But if this is how it ends, we should've been more fearless

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.250
I'm sorry, please don't misunderstand me.
I didn't mean to imply you were a problem...

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.040
No... it's okay! I'm sorry.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:59.080
We should have spent all that time laughing together,

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.500
I'm going to work hard!

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:56.710
Huh?

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:00.590
Work hard... and focus everything on the job
in front of me right now!

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.710
The two of us

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:06.420
When this swaying train starts moving,

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:03.120
Then after that...!

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:09.840
Then after that... someday, once again,
I'll become your editor.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:09.840
I hear from beyond the window

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:13.630
Gotansha Publishing

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.080
Mayu!

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.080
This is the paper you were looking for, isn't it?

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:20.050
Senpai, please hold on to it for me.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:21.710
Huh?

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:24.710
In exchange... I'll be holding on to this for you.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:26.380
What's that?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.330
WAIT! IS THAT...?!

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.460
You sure have some BIG aspirations!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.500
Ah! Wait! Give it back!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.750
No way!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.250
Nagisa!
How embarrassing!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.880
Quit horsing around. We're going.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.040
Yessir!

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.670
Hold on, Mayu!

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.370
Well then, Senpai, I've got work to do.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.210
Hey! That...

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.870
Don't show it to anybody!

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:57.260
Someday...

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.630
Until I reach my goal...

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:02.920
To inspire me to become the best
at accomplishing the job in front of me...

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:05.080
Hurry up.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:07.830
I'll hold on to this as a good luck charm!

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.510
Shangri-la

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:37.750
Yume no naka de sae umaku waraenai kimi no koto

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:43.080
Dame na hitotte shikari nagara aishiteitai

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:50.040
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:53.620
Bokura doko he mukaouka

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:59.090
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.340
Shangri-la

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:06.290
Shiawasedatte sakende kureyo

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:10.580
Ijippari na kimi no nakigao misete kureyo

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.250
Shangri-la

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.250
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai boku no koto

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:22.290
Dame na hitotte shikarinagara ashitekure

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:25.500
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.830
Next Episode: Princess Man
